                <pb facs="0464" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/8–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-04T17:00:00+03:25">August 4, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 4—2:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>577. Petroleum concession negotiations have reached point at which I believe it
                    imperative that American companies send representatives from highest executive
                    level to complete presentation of bids, if an American firm is to get
                    concession. Representatives should be empowered to make decisions on spot
                    without reference to home office.</p>
                <p>May I urge upon Department utmost necessity of prevailing upon companies to get
                    their men to Tehran without delay. Competent authorities state prospects of
                    proposed concession area have no equal in Middle East, but to gain this rich
                    prize for American interests will require quick action, including granting of
                    number one air priorities for top caliber negotiators with full powers.</p>
                <p>I am reliably informed that one bid or another will be accepted by Cabinet and
                    presented to Majlis for approval by September 1.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
